r quiet option, but (A, 3) offers better structural connectivity.\n\nReason: I chose (A, 3) to maximize stability and minimize the opponent\'s tactical responses. By flipping only piece B4, I avoid opening up too many new moves for the opponent (a concept known as evaporation or minimizing frontier). This move also establishes a safe presence on the top edge and reinforces the vertical control of column 3, whereas other valid moves risk creating unbalanced formations or over-flipping pieces too early.\n\nAnswer: (A, 3)'}
