is is a "loud" move that creates a solid wall of your pieces, which often gives the opponent a surface to play against (e.g., enabling F1), so it is strategically weaker.\n\nReason: The move (D, 1) is chosen because it is the best "quiet move" available. It flips only a single opponent piece, which preserves your tactical advantage by not opening up new frontiers for the opponent. Furthermore, it claims a spot on the edge (Column 1), which is generally valuable for long-term stability.\n\nAnswer: (D, 1)'}
